    {
     "text": "THE DOUBLE CROSS SYSTEM",
     "y": 1059,
     "size": 27,
     "underline": 26
    },
    {
     "para": "In 1940, MI5 pulls off an extraordinary feat: almost every spy Germany sends to England is spotted and arrested. Once caught, they have only one choice: cooperate, or face British justice.",
     "y": 1113
    },
    {
     "para": "Those who agree keep writing to their German handlers. But every message is drafted in London by a secret committee, the Twenty Committee. In Roman numerals, twenty is written XX: the “double cross”.",
     "y": 1255
    },
    {
     "para": "Berlin believes it has a vast network in England. In reality, the entire network works for the British.",
     "y": 1407
    }
   ]
  },
